            <span class="t-prompt">$</span> npm install @astralbeam/sdk
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-demo reveal" style="--reveal-delay:.3s">
          <aside class="panel agent-panel" id="agent-demo">
            <header class="agent-bar mono">
              <span class="agent-title">ACME ASSISTANT</span>
              <button class="agent-replay mono" type="button" data-replay>
                <svg class="icon-replay" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M13.6 8a5.6 5.6 0 1 1-1.7-4"></path>
                  <path d="M12.6 1.3v3.2H9.4"></path>
                </svg>
                REPLAY
              </button>
            </header>

            <div class="agent-thread" data-thread>
              <article class="agent-msg is-user" data-step>
                <p>Refund order 4821 and let the customer know.</p>
              </article>
              <article class="agent-msg is-agent" data-step>
                <ul class="agent-tools mono">
                  <li class="agent-tool" data-tool>
                    <i class="tool-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="tool-name">lookupOrder</span><b>4821</b>
                  </li>
                  <li class="agent-tool" data-tool>
                    <i class="tool-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="tool-name">refundOrder</span><b>$128.00</b>
                  </li>
                  <li class="agent-tool" data-tool>
                    <i class="tool-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="tool-name">sendEmail</span><b>receipt</b>
                  </li>
                </ul>
                <!-- The host's own <OrderCard /> widget, drawn inside the reply. -->
                <div class="agent-widget" data-widget>
                  <header class="widget-head mono">
                    <span>ORDER 4821</span>
                    <span class="widget-badge">REFUNDED</span>
                  </header>
                  <dl class="widget-rows mono">
                    <div>
                      <dt>Customer</dt>
                      <dd>Dana Whitfield</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <dt>Total</dt>
                      <dd>$128.00</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <dt>Card</dt>
                      <dd>Visa ···4242</dd>
                    </div>
                  </dl>
                </div>
                <p class="agent-stream" data-stream>
                  Refunded $128.00 and emailed Dana the confirmation.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article class="agent-msg is-user" data-step>
                <a class="agent-attachment mono" href="/demo/returns-q3.csv" download
                  title="Download the sample file">
                  <svg class="icon-file" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path d="M4 1.5h5.5L13 5v9.5H4z"></path>
                    <path d="M9.5 1.5V5H13"></path>
                  </svg>
                  returns-q3.csv <b>41 rows</b>
                </a>
                <p>Which of these returns are still unpaid? Put them in a spreadsheet.</p>
              </article>
              <article class="agent-msg is-agent" data-step>
                <ul class="agent-tools mono">
                  <li class="agent-tool" data-tool>
                    <i class="tool-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="tool-name">readAttachment</span><b>returns-q3.csv</b>
                  </li>
                  <li class="agent-tool" data-tool>
                    <i class="tool-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="tool-name">sandbox</span><b>python unpaid.py</b>
                  </li>
                </ul>
                <!-- A sandbox artifact, published as a signed download. -->
                <a class="agent-widget agent-artifact mono" data-widget
                  href="/demo/unpaid-returns.xlsx" download title="Download the sample spreadsheet">
                  <svg class="icon-file" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path d="M4 1.5h5.5L13 5v9.5H4z"></path>
                    <path d="M9.5 1.5V5H13"></path>
                  </svg>
                  <span class="artifact-name">unpaid-returns.xlsx</span>
                  <span class="artifact-size">17 KB</span>
                  <span class="artifact-download" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
                </a>
                <p class="agent-stream" data-stream>
                  3 of 41 returns are still unpaid, $612 in total. The spreadsheet is ready to download.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article class="agent-msg is-user" data-step>
                <p>How have refunds trended over the last six weeks?</p>
              </article>
              <article class="agent-msg is-agent" data-step>
                <ul class="agent-tools mono">
                  <li class="agent-tool" data-tool>
                    <i class="tool-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="tool-name">refundsByWeek</span><b>6 weeks</b>
                  </li>
                </ul>
                <!-- The host's own <RefundsChart /> widget: one series, peak week emphasized. -->
                <figure class="agent-widget agent-chart" data-widget>
                  <figcaption class="widget-head mono">
                    <span>REFUNDS BY WEEK</span>
                    <span class="chart-total">$8,200</span>
                  </figcaption>
                  <div class="chart-plot" role="img" aria-label="Refunds by week: week 33 $1,180, week 34 $2,140, week 35 $1,760, week 36 $1,320, week 37 $980, week 38 $820.">
                    <div class="chart-col" style="--v:55%">
                      <i class="chart-bar" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="chart-col is-peak" style="--v:100%">
                      <b class="chart-value mono">$2,140</b>
                      <i class="chart-bar" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="chart-col" style="--v:82%">
                      <i class="chart-bar" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="chart-col" style="--v:62%">
                      <i class="chart-bar" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="chart-col" style="--v:46%">
                      <i class="chart-bar" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="chart-col" style="--v:38%">
                      <i class="chart-bar" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <ul class="chart-ticks mono">
                    <li>W33</li>
                    <li>W34</li>
                    <li>W35</li>
                    <li>W36</li>
                    <li>W37</li>
                    <li>W38</li>
                  </ul>
                </figure>
                <p class="agent-stream" data-stream>
                  Refunds peaked at $2,140 in week 34 after the carrier delay, then fell 62% by week 38.
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>

            <form class="agent-composer" data-composer>
              <input
                class="agent-input"
                type="text"
                autocomplete="off"
                placeholder="Ask the agent…"
                aria-label="Ask the demo agent"
                data-input
              />
              <button class="agent-send" type="submit" aria-label="Send message">↑</button>
            </form>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>

      <a class="scroll-cue" href="#step-01" aria-label="Skip to the next section">
        <i class="scroll-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      </a>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ STEPS ============ -->
    {
      steps.map((step) => (
        <section class="section step" id={`step-${step.index}`}>
          <div class="section-head">
            <p class="step-index mono reveal">STEP {step.index}</p>
            <h2 class="display section-title reveal scramble" data-text={step.title}>
              {step.title}
            </h2>
            <p class="section-sub reveal">{step.desc}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <div class="panel terminal reveal" data-terminal>
              <header class="terminal-bar mono">
                <span class="term-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
                <span>{step.file}</span>
              </header>
              <pre class="terminal-body mono" aria-label={`Step ${step.index} code`}><code set:html={highlight(step.code)} /><span class="t-caret" aria-hidden="true"></span></pre>
            </div>
            <ul class="benefits">
              {
                step.benefits.map((benefit, i) => (
                  <li class="panel benefit reveal" style={`--reveal-delay:${(i % 2) * 0.1 + 0.1}s`}>
                    <h3 class="benefit-name">{benefit.name}</h3>
                    <p class="benefit-desc">{benefit.desc}</p>
                    {benefit.soon && (
                      <p class="benefit-status">
                        <span class="tag mono">IN PROGRESS</span>
                      </p>
                    )}
                    <i class="panel-corner" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                  </li>
                ))
              }
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>
      ))
    }

    <!-- ============ INTEGRATIONS ============ -->
    <section class="section" id="integrations">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="display section-title reveal scramble" data-text="WORKS WITH YOUR STACK">
          WORKS WITH YOUR STACK
        </h2>
        <p class="section-sub reveal">
          AstralBeam sits between your app and the providers you already pay for. Swap any of them
          without touching the widget.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="integrations-grid">
        {
          integrations.map((group, i) => (
            <div class="panel integration-panel reveal" style={`--reveal-delay:${(i % 2) * 0.1}s`}>
              <h3 class="integration-label mono">{group.label}</h3>
              <p class="integration-desc">{group.desc}</p>
              <ul class="chips mono">
                {
                  group.items.map((item) => (
                    <li class={item.soon ? "chip is-soon" : "chip"} title={item.soon ? "In progress" : undefined}>
                      {item.name}
                    </li>
                  ))
                }
              </ul>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ OPEN SOURCE ============ -->
    <section class="section" id="open-source">
      <svg class="os-watermark" viewBox="-84 -62 168 124" aria-hidden="true">
        <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
          <path d="M -6.56 -18.02 A 30 34 0 1 0 -6.56 18.02"></path>
          <ellipse cx="32" cy="0" rx="30" ry="34"></ellipse>
          <path
            transform="rotate(22)"
            d="M 0 -56 C 4 -50 6.5 -42 6.5 -31 L 6.5 31 C 6.5 42 4 50 0 56 C -4 50 -6.5 42 -6.5 31 L -6.5 -31 C -6.5 -42 -4 -50 0 -56 Z"
          ></path>
        </g>
      </svg>

      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="display section-title reveal scramble" data-text="OPEN SOURCE FROM DAY ONE">
          OPEN SOURCE FROM DAY ONE
        </h2>
        <p class="section-sub reveal">
          The AstralBeam platform is open source under AGPL-3.0, built on open standards, and
          modular by design. Read it, fork it, run it, extend it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="os-grid">
        <div class="panel os-panel reveal">
          <h3 class="os-name mono">SELF-HOST</h3>
          <p>Run the whole platform on your own infrastructure. Your data never leaves your orbit.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel os-panel reveal" style="--reveal-delay:.1s">
          <h3 class="os-name mono">CLOUD</h3>
          <p>Let us run it for you: managed infrastructure, zero maintenance, always current.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel os-panel reveal" style="--reveal-delay:.2s">
          <h3 class="os-name mono">MODULAR</h3>
          <p>Start with the entire platform, or adopt it incrementally, piece by piece.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel os-panel reveal" style="--reveal-delay:.3s">
          <h3 class="os-name mono">OPEN PROTOCOLS</h3>
          <p>Built on open protocols: AG-UI, MCP, A2A. Swap pieces in and out instead of adopting a proprietary runtime.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="os-repo reveal" style="--reveal-delay:.35s">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={githubUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <svg class="icon-social" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 0a8 8 0 0 0-2.53 15.59c.4.07.55-.17.55-.38l-.01-1.34c-2.23.48-2.7-1.07-2.7-1.07-.36-.93-.89-1.18-.89-1.18-.73-.5.05-.49.05-.49.8.06 1.23.83 1.23.83.72 1.23 1.88.87 2.34.67.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82a7.6 7.6 0 0 1 4 0c1.53-1.03 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.28.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48l-.01 2.2c0 .21.14.46.55.38A8 8 0 0 0 8 0z"></path></svg>
          BROWSE THE SOURCE
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={`${docsUrl}/self-hosting`}>
          SELF-HOSTING GUIDE
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ LAUNCH ============ -->
    <section class="section launch" id="launch">
      <h2 class="display launch-title reveal scramble"
        data-text="READY FOR LAUNCH">READY FOR LAUNCH</h2>
      <p class="section-sub launch-sub reveal">
        Get started with a few lines of code, <span>or come talk to us on Discord.</span>
